  "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6-2x)=$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6-2x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14246608/assets/bba697be09903e54cffc4bf0c0e05cbd30cbfc11975cac5097e964415baca113.png)\n\nThe function is not defined for $x>3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6-2x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$\n\nHowever, the function is defined for $x<3.$ Moreover,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6-2x)=-\\infty .\n$$",
